  "change": "SvgGaussianDeviation owns the inclusive 0.03f image-alias cutoff and its classification. Kernel copying has an explicitly separate HasIdentityKernel query. Bounds, alias resolution, sampling, storage and primitive materialization consume the shared rule.",
  "preserved": [
    "Mapped deviations retain their original float narrowing and finite admission; pre-admission alias classification still accepts absolute mapped values without constructing a validated deviation.",
    "A copying pixel kernel can materialize an image. Both original boundary vectors (0.03f and its immediate successor) retain their distinct storage classifications and assert copying-kernel identity.",
    "Capture hints retain 3*sigma; backward requests retain ceil(3*sigma), including effective-zero aliases; stored bounds retain per-axis cutoff and integer enclosure. No rounding stage is merged.",
    "Source maps, clipping, sampling, color transfer, alpha rounding, text layout, allocations and ownership are unchanged. No native source, reference, tolerance, public API or dependency changes."
  ],
